cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite the article and this deposit."
title: "quasar: quantum simulation of mutation-selection dynamics"
version: 1.0.0
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ahmedanees-m/quasar"
abstract: >-
  Code, protocol, result records and raw quantum-processor measurements for a study of whether
  quantum algorithms help compute the quasispecies distribution of molecular evolution. Two
  quantum routes are benchmarked against three compute-matched classical baselines across 777
  problem instances, and the error-threshold sweep is executed on a superconducting processor.
  No advantage is found at the sizes tested, and the obstruction is shown to be structural.
keywords:
  - quantum algorithms
  - quasispecies
  - mutation-selection dynamics
  - imaginary-time evolution
  - tensor networks
  - quantum-classical boundary
  - reproducible research
  - negative result
